  "id": "Compound::DB01026 - Gene::1559",
  "verbalization": "Ketoconazole is implicated in the regulation of Cyp2c9 through multiple indirect pathways, primarily through its interaction with other enzymes and compounds. The evidence suggests that Ketoconazole may influence Cyp2c9 via the binding of related compounds, such as Ritonavir and Miconazole, which in turn bind to Cyp2c9. This indicates a potential mechanism where Ketoconazole indirectly modulates Cyp2c9 through the metabolic activation of other substances. Additionally, the presence of Leflunomide, which binds to Cyp2c9, further supports the notion that Ketoconazole may contribute to the regulation of Cyp2c9 through a chain of interactions involving other drugs and enzymes. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the metabolic interactions involving Cyp2c9 and underscores the role of Ketoconazole in the broader context of drug metabolism and enzyme regulation.",
